{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And HaShem was angry with me for your sakes.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: if you cross over into the land, they will say — what was decreed upon the wilderness generation, that they not enter the land, was because they have no share in the World to Come; and if you enter the land through your prayer, they will say — Moses cared only about himself. Rather, you will be buried among them and bring them with you to the future — this is ״and you will gather the heads of the people״ (ושמת בארצם)." "<b>It is enough for you.</b> With what I have shown you — the conquest of the land of Sihon and Og — since you said 'Let me cross over.' <b>Do not continue to speak to Me further about this matter.</b> And since you said 'Let me see the good land' — I heed you: ascend the summit of the peak, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is textually difficult. The final phrase reads 'ותביא עמך לעתיד היינו ויתא ראשי עם' — 'ותא/ושמת ראשי עם' apparently alludes to Deut 3:28 'וצוה את יהושע וחזקהו ואמצהו כי הוא יעבר לפני העם'. The verse reference embedded in the comment appears garbled; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:46.116153387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}